docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:87:## Flow 6: Risk rule editing (desktop, rare, deliberate)
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:91:No bulk edit. No editing while a halt is active (prevents mood-driven loosening on a bad day; the halt banner says so).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:93:## Flow 7: Watchlist
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:97:## Flow 8: System health & kill switch
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:99:Token age (days:hours, with the Sunday cadence marked), last successful sync per feed, recent job failures, API spend this month. One control: **Pause system** (kill switch): stops all proposal creation and submission until unpaused. Unpause requires typed confirmation.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:101:## Cross-cutting states
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:104:- **Stale data:** any market number older than its cache window shows a staleness mark with timestamp. Never render a price without its age being discoverable.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:105:- **Token expired:** global banner, read-only mode for anything requiring fresh Schwab data.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:106:- **Empty states:** pre-first-sync dashboard, empty journal, empty queue each need a designed state (the queue's empty state is the normal state most of the time).
