     1	# Phase 1 Plan: Investment Copilot (read-only)
     2	
     3	Source of truth: `docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md` (v9). Screen states from `docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md` and the wireframes. This plan covers only PRD §6 Phase 1 as scoped in the kickoff brief.
     4	
     5	Sections: decisions needed before code, migrations, jobs, MCP tools, scheduled runtime, UI, testing, deploy, build order, deferred items, working method.
     6	
     7	---
     8	
     9	## 0. Decisions (resolved 2026-09-01)
    10	
    11	1. **Secrets in Rails credentials**, production-only file (`config/credentials/production.yml.enc`), keys `schwab.app_key`, `schwab.app_secret`, `mcp.bearer_token`, `anthropic.api_key`, `resend.api_key`, plus Active Record Encryption keys. `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL` and `MEMORY_REPO_PATH` stay in dokku ENV (not secret). The dokku `SCHWAB_APP_KEY`/`SCHWAB_APP_SECRET` vars get unset once the credentials file is on the server.
    12	2. **Gems beyond defaults:** `rspec-rails`, `factory_bot_rails`, `vcr`, `webmock`, `bundler-audit`, `mcp` (official Ruby SDK), `anthropic` (official Ruby SDK). No claude-on-rails.
    13	3. **Web login is passwordless magic link**, built on the Rails 8 auth generator with `generates_token_for :magic_link` (15 min, single use). Users are seeded, not self-registered: john@athayde.com and whitney@athayde.com only. No gem.
    14	4. **Email via Resend over SMTP**, no gem; API key in credentials. Production login and re-auth depend on it, so Resend DNS is a prerequisite for the first production deploy.
    15	5. **`evaluate_hypothetical_order` omitted** from Phase 1. `get_risk_rules` ships and returns the (empty) `risk_rules` rows.
    16	6. **§5.12 allocation tables deferred** to Phase 2.5.
    17	7. **Off-hours cadence** for orders/transactions sync: hourly.
    18	
    19	---
    20	
    21	## 1. Migrations (in creation order)
    22	
    23	All money columns `decimal(18,4)`, quantities `decimal(18,6)` (fractional shares unverified, PRD §5.12). All timestamps `timestamptz`. No table stores a bare ticker as a key; instrument references are `instrument_id`.
    24	
    25	| # | Table | Key columns | Phase 1 populated? |
    26	|---|---|---|---|
    27	| 1 | `users`, `sessions` | Rails 8 auth generator, password column removed; `email_address` unique. Magic-link tokens via `generates_token_for`, no table. | yes (two seeded users) |
    28	| 2 | `schwab_tokens` | `access_token` (encrypted), `refresh_token` (encrypted), `access_expires_at`, `refresh_expires_at`, `issued_at`, `last_refreshed_at`, `last_refresh_error`, `scope` | yes |
    29	| 3 | `accounts` | `encrypted_hash_id` (Schwab's hashValue, unique), `account_type` enum (taxable/ira), `trading_enabled` bool, `nickname`, `last_synced_at`. Plaintext number is never a column. | yes |
    30	| 4 | `instruments` | `cusip` (unique, not null), `symbol`, `symbol_history` jsonb `[{symbol, seen_at}]`, `asset_type`, `leveraged` bool default false, `description`. Index on `symbol` (non-unique). | yes |
    31	| 5 | `positions` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `quantity`, `average_price`, `cost_basis`, `market_value`, `last_price`, `synced_at`, `raw` jsonb. Unique on (account, instrument). Always overwritten by sync, never edited. | yes |
    32	| 6 | `balances` | `account_id`, `equity`, `cash_available_for_trading`, `settled_cash`, `unsettled_cash`, `buying_power`, `synced_at`, `raw` jsonb. One current row per account plus history (`as_of` date). | yes |
    33	| 7 | `orders` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `broker_order_id` (unique per account), `status` enum incl. Phase 2 states, `side`, `quantity`, `filled_quantity`, `order_type`, `limit_price`, `stop_price`, `duration`, `session`, `tax_lot_method`, `placed_via` enum (schwab_direct/app), `parent_order_id` (self FK), `order_proposal_id` (nullable), `entered_at`, `closed_at`, `raw` jsonb | yes (sync only) |
    34	| 8 | `order_proposals` | Full §5.2 shape now: `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `origin` enum (agent/human), `status` enum (proposed, validated, rejected, approved, submitted, submission_unknown, filled, cancelled), `side`, `quantity`, `order_type`, `limit_price`, `stop_price`, `target_price`, `thesis`, `setup_id`, `guardrail_results` jsonb, `risk_rule_version`, `override_reason`, `reject_reason`, `submission_attempted_at`, `submission_payload` jsonb, `submission_response` jsonb, `reconciled_order_id`, `approved_at`, `submitted_at` | no |
    35	| 9 | `transactions` | `account_id`, `instrument_id` (nullable for cash-only), `broker_transaction_id` (unique), `kind` enum (fill, dividend, interest, fee, deposit, withdrawal, corporate_action, other), `sub_type` string (raw Schwab type), `side`, `quantity`, `price`, `net_amount`, `settlement_date`, `executed_at`, `raw` jsonb, `journaled_at` | yes |
    36	| 10 | `setups` | `name` (unique), `definition`, `active` bool, `win_rate`, `avg_r`, `expectancy`, `sample_size`, `stats_computed_at` | table yes, rows via seed |
    37	| 11 | `trades` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `setup_id` (nullable), `order_proposal_id` (nullable), `status` enum (open, closed, incomplete), `opened_at`, `closed_at`, `avg_entry`, `avg_exit`, `peak_quantity`, `planned_stop`, `planned_target`, `realized_pnl`, `realized_r`, `thesis`, `post_mortem`, `followed_setup` (nullable bool) | yes |
    38	| 12 | `trade_legs` | `trade_id`, `transaction_id` (unique), `direction` enum (in/out), `quantity`, `price`, `executed_at`, `basis_adjustment` (for corporate actions/dividend reinvest) | yes |
    39	| 13 | `risk_rules` | `rule_type`, `params` jsonb, `active`, `version`, `setup_id` (nullable, for collar params), `superseded_by_id` | no |
    40	| 14 | `snapshots` | `as_of` date (unique), `equity`, `net_flows` (day), `cumulative_net_flows`, `flow_adjusted_equity`, `high_water_mark` (on adjusted series), `drawdown_pct`, `open_risk_amount`, `open_risk_pct` | yes (open risk is 0 until stops exist; column stays) |
    41	| 15 | `audit_events` | `kind` string, `actor` enum (human/system/agent), `subject` polymorphic (nullable), `data` jsonb, `reason`, `created_at` only. Postgres trigger rejects UPDATE/DELETE. | yes |
    42	| 16 | `market_days` | `date` (unique), `open` bool, `opens_at`, `closes_at`, `raw` jsonb, `fetched_at`. Populated from Schwab market-hours endpoint. | yes |
    43	| 17 | `sync_runs` | `feed` enum (accounts, positions, balances, orders, transactions, market_hours, memory_repo), `status` (running, succeeded, failed, skipped_token), `started_at`, `finished_at`, `error`, `records_touched`. Drives "last successful sync per feed" on health screen. | yes |
    44	| 18 | `agent_runs` | `kind` enum (morning_brief, eod, sunday_review), `status`, `started_at`, `finished_at`, `tool_turns`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `estimated_cost`, `output_markdown`, `error`, `model` | yes |
    45	| 19 | `system_settings` | Singleton row: `shadow_mode` bool default true, `manual_halt` bool default false, `manual_halt_reason`, `manual_halt_at` | yes |
    46	
    47	Also the Solid Queue / Cache / Cable schemas already generated. Active Record Encryption keys go in the production credentials file (generated with `bin/rails db:encryption:init`); dev/test use fixed keys in their own credentials files.
    48	
    49	Phase 2 columns are present now so `orders`/`order_proposals` never need a shape change: `parent_order_id`, `order_proposal_id`, `submission_unknown` state, submission attempt columns, `guardrail_results`, `risk_rule_version`.
    50	
    51	---
    52	
    53	## 2. Jobs (Solid Queue, `config/recurring.yml`, all times America/New_York)
    54	
    55	Every Schwab-touching job includes `TokenGated`: if the refresh token is expired it writes a `sync_runs` row with `skipped_token`, audits once per expiry episode, and re-enqueues itself for 15 minutes later. Nothing silently skips.
    56	
    57	| Job | Schedule | Does |
    58	|---|---|---|
    59	| `Schwab::RefreshAccessTokenJob` | every 25 min | POST refresh grant; update `schwab_tokens`; on failure audit `token_refresh_failed` |
    60	| `Schwab::TokenHealthJob` | daily 08:00 + 20:00 | Email nag when refresh token < 24h from expiry; escalations Mon and Tue if Sunday re-auth missed; audit each nag |
    61	| `Sync::MarketHoursJob` | daily 06:00, and on demand when `market_days` lacks today | Fetch equity market hours for today and the next 7 days into `market_days` |
    62	| `Sync::TickJob` | every 5 min | The only scheduled sync entry point. Consults `MarketCalendar` + `sync_runs` and enqueues: positions+balances if due (15 min in-hours, 60 min otherwise); orders+transactions if due (5 min in-hours, 60 min otherwise) |
    63	| `Sync::AccountsJob` | daily 06:05 and after every re-auth | `/accounts/accountNumbers` then `/accounts`; upsert `accounts` by hash |
    64	| `Sync::PositionsJob` | via tick | `/accounts/{hash}?fields=positions`; upsert instruments (CUSIP), positions, balances |
    65	| `Sync::OrdersJob` | via tick | `/accounts/{hash}/orders?fromEnteredTime=…`; upsert orders, set `placed_via: schwab_direct` when no proposal matches |
    66	| `Sync::TransactionsJob` | via tick | `/accounts/{hash}/transactions`; upsert transactions, classify kind; then enqueue `Journal::LinkFillsJob` |
    67	| `Journal::LinkFillsJob` | after transactions sync | Zero-to-zero trade builder (see §4 below) |
    68	| `Snapshots::DailyJob` | 16:20 on market days, after final sync | Write the day's snapshot with flow adjustment |
    69	| `Memory::PullRepoJob` | every 30 min | `git -C $MEMORY_REPO_PATH pull --ff-only`; record `sync_runs` |
    70	| `Agent::MorningBriefJob` | 07:00 market days | See §3 |
    71	| `Agent::EndOfDayJob` | 16:30 market days | See §3 |
    72	| `Agent::SundayReviewJob` | Sunday 18:00 | Phase 1 stub: emails re-auth link, token age, sync health, job failures |
    73	
    74	---
    75	
    76	## 3. Tool surface (one registry, two transports)
    77	
    78	`app/models/agent/tools/*` each defines `name`, `description`, `input_schema`, `call(**args)`. The MCP server registers them; the scheduled runtime passes the same definitions to the Messages API. Phase 1 tools, all read-only:
    79	
    80	| Tool | Returns |
    81	|---|---|
    82	| `get_portfolio` | Positions with last price, unrealized P&L, working stop (nil in Phase 1), distance to stop (nil), open risk, synced_at per row |
    83	| `get_account_health` | Equity, settled/unsettled cash, drawdown from HWM, token status and age, last sync per feed, shadow mode, halt state |
    84	| `get_quotes(symbols)` | Schwab `/marketdata/v1/quotes`, cached 2 min in Solid Cache, each quote stamped with fetched_at |
    85	| `get_price_history(symbol, range)` | Schwab `/marketdata/v1/pricehistory`, cached 5 min |
    86	| `get_journal(filters)` | Trades with legs; filters: status, setup, instrument, date range, missing_post_mortem |
    87	| `get_setup_stats` | Rows from `setups` with rolling stats recomputed from `trades` |
    88	| `get_risk_rules` | Active `risk_rules` rows (empty in Phase 1) |
    89	
    90	Omitted pending decision 0.5: `evaluate_hypothetical_order`. Write tools do not exist in Phase 1.
    91	
    92	**MCP server:** `POST /mcp` (Streamable HTTP, JSON-RPC 2.0), bearer token compared with `ActiveSupport::SecurityUtils.secure_compare`, 401 renders a plain "MCP auth failed" page (Playwright target). Every tool call writes an `audit_events` row (`mcp_tool_called`, actor: agent).
    93	
    94	**Scheduled runtime:** `Agent::Run` wraps one Messages API conversation: system prompt = memory repo markdown files + setup stats + token health; tools = registry above; hard cap `MAX_TOOL_TURNS = 12`; result stored in `agent_runs` and emailed via `BriefMailer`. Prompts live in `app/models/agent/prompts/*.md.erb`. Morning brief and EOD are real; Sunday review stub does not call the API.
    95	
    96	---
    97	
    98	## 4. Journal builder (zero-to-zero)
    99	
   100	For each account and instrument, process fills in `executed_at` order:
   101	- No open trade and a buy fill: open a trade. If the fill's order maps to a proposal, copy setup/thesis/planned stop; otherwise `status: incomplete`, no planned stop.
   102	- Each fill becomes a `trade_leg` (in/out by side). Running quantity updated; `avg_entry`/`avg_exit` recomputed.
   103	- Running quantity returns to zero: close the trade, compute `realized_pnl`; `realized_r` only when `planned_stop` exists, else nil.
   104	- Dividends and corporate actions with a CUSIP link to the open trade as a `basis_adjustment` leg; symbol changes on a known CUSIP update `instruments.symbol` and append to `symbol_history` without touching trades.
   105	- Idempotent: keyed on `transactions.id` via the unique index on `trade_legs.transaction_id`.
   106	
   107	---
   108	
   109	## 5. UI (Hotwire, mobile-responsive, no JS routers, no hover-dependent modals)
   110	
   111	| Screen | Route | Phase 1 content |
   112	|---|---|---|
   113	| Dashboard | `/` | Banner (healthy / expiring / expired / halted), equity + day change, open risk, settled/unsettled cash, positions list (distance-to-stop column shows "no stop" in Phase 1), pending proposals count (0, links nowhere yet), staleness stamps on every number, empty state before first sync |
   114	| System health | `/system` | Token age vs 7d, next Sunday, last sync per feed, job failures (7d), API spend (month, from `agent_runs`), shadow mode indicator, manual halt toggle with reason (audited) |
   115	| Re-auth | `/schwab/authorize` → Schwab → `/schwab/callback` | Success page with new expiry; failure page with error and retry |
   116	| Journal (minimal) | `/trades`, `/trades/:id` | List and detail; the Flow 4 quick-entry form (post-mortem + followed/improvised) so incomplete trades can be completed |
   117	| Login | `/session/new` → email → `/session/magic/:token` | Passwordless; unknown emails get the same "check your inbox" response |
   118	
   119	Banner precedence: halted > expired > expiring > healthy. Halted in Phase 1 comes only from `system_settings.manual_halt`.
   120	
   121	---
   122	
   123	## 6. Testing
   124	
   125	- **RSpec**, in the kickoff's priority order: token lifecycle with `travel_to`; sync jobs with fixture payloads (positions, orders, transactions incl. dividend, split, symbol change); journal linking (scale-in/out, orphan fill → incomplete, ticker change on same CUSIP); MCP tool contracts (request specs for auth + each tool's schema and output); scheduled runtime with a stubbed Messages API (tool-turn cap enforced).
   126	- **VCR cassettes** in `spec/cassettes`, recorded against Schwab only once the app is Ready For Use, with a scrubber that replaces bearer tokens, refresh tokens, and account hash values before write. Until then, cassettes are hand-built from community-client response shapes and marked `# SCHWAB_SHAPE_UNVERIFIED`.
   127	- **`Schwab::FakeClient`** implements the same interface as `Schwab::Client`, returns canned payloads, selected by `config.x.schwab.adapter`. Used by dev seeds and Playwright.
   128	- **Playwright** (`e2e/`, `@playwright/test` via npm, the only Node dependency): dashboard in four banner states via a test-env-only `/playwright/scenarios/:name` reseed route, MCP 401 page, re-auth success and failure (FakeClient scripted).
   129	- **`bin/ci`**: Rails 8.1 `ActiveSupport::ContinuousIntegration` with steps in `config/ci.rb`, the pattern borrowed from Patchvault. Kickoff order: rubocop → rspec → brakeman (strict, warnings fail) → `bin/importmap audit` → `bundle exec bundle-audit check --update` → Playwright (`bin/playwright`, which boots a test-env server with the FakeClient, runs `npx playwright test`, and tears down). Fails on the first red step.
   130	
   131	---
   132	
   133	## 7. Deploy
   134	
   135	- `Procfile`: `web: bundle exec puma -C config/puma.rb`, `worker: bin/jobs`, `release: bin/rails db:prepare`.
   136	- `app.json` for the release phase.
   137	- `bin/dokku-setup`: documents postgres plugin, letsencrypt, config vars (`RAILS_MASTER_KEY`, `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL`, `MEMORY_REPO_PATH`, plus whatever decision 0.1 leaves in ENV), storage mount for the memory repo, `ps:scale worker=1`.
   138	- App time zone `Eastern Time (US & Canada)`; Solid Queue recurring schedules use the same.
   139	
   140	---
   141	
   142	## 8. Build order (green `bin/ci` at each step)
   143	
   144	1. Tooling: RSpec, rubocop config, brakeman, bundler-audit, `bin/ci` (without Playwright), authentication generator, AR encryption keys, credentials layout.
   145	2. Migrations 1–19, models with validations/enums, `AuditEvent` append-only trigger, `SystemSettings` singleton.
   146	3. Schwab adapter: `Schwab::Client` (OAuth, accounts, positions, orders, transactions, market hours, quotes, price history), `Schwab::FakeClient`, response mappers, `docs/verify-on-approval.md` started.
   147	4. OAuth controller + token model + refresh job + token health job + re-auth pages + audit events.
   148	5. Sync jobs, market calendar, tick scheduler, `sync_runs`.
   149	6. Journal builder + snapshots.
   150	7. Dashboard, system health, journal screens; Playwright added to `bin/ci`.
   151	8. MCP server + tool registry.
   152	9. Scheduled runtime + mailers + memory repo pull.
   153	10. Seeds for dev via FakeClient; `Procfile`, `app.json`, `bin/dokku-setup`; DHH-skill review pass.
   154	
   155	---
   156	
   157	## 9. Explicitly not built in Phase 1
   158	
   159	Guardrail engine, order proposals (table only), approval UI, submission, brackets, reconciliation job, allocation module, FMP, watchlist screen (watchlist.md in the memory repo is read as text), push notifications, iOS shell.
   160	
   161	---
   162	
   163	## 10. Working method, per phase and per build step
   164	
   165	Each numbered step in §8 that ships a feature runs this loop:
   166	
   167	1. **PRD review with counselors** (`counselors run`, agents `codex-5.5-high` and `claude-fable`): the relevant PRD sections plus this plan's section for the step. Findings are folded into the plan before code.
   168	2. **Build** the feature vertically per §8.
   169	3. **RSpec green** and reviewed for coverage against the §6 priority list, not just passing.
   170	4. **DHH skill review pass** (`dhh-code-reviewer` agent) on the step's diff; fix what it flags.
   171	5. **Counselors review of the build** (same two agents) on the diff; fix or explicitly decline each finding in the commit message.
   172	6. **`bin/ci` green.** Commit.
   173	
   174	Counselors runs are long (10 to 20 minutes) and run in the background while unrelated work continues. Whole-phase gates: a counselors PRD review before step 1, and a DHH pass plus counselors review over the full Phase 1 diff after step 10.

