     1	# Investment Copilot: UI Flows & Information Architecture
     2	
     3	Companion to the PRD (§5.8). This is what the UI must do, not how it looks. Screens, flows, states, and the data each screen owns. Mobile-first where marked; everything renders on a phone, but some screens only need to be *usable* there, not optimized.
     4	
     5	## Actors and entry points
     6	
     7	One user. Three ways in:
     8	
     9	1. **Push/email notification** → deep link to a specific proposal, trade, or health alert. This is the primary mobile entry.
    10	2. **Direct visit** → dashboard.
    11	3. **Sunday email** → re-auth link and edge review link.
    12	
    13	## Screen inventory
    14	
    15	| Screen | Priority surface | Purpose |
    16	|---|---|---|
    17	| Dashboard | Mobile + desktop | Glanceable state of the book |
    18	| Proposal detail | **Mobile-first** | The approve/reject decision |
    19	| Proposal queue | Mobile + desktop | List of pending/recent proposals |
    20	| New proposal (manual) | Mobile + desktop | Human-initiated order proposal |
    21	| Trade detail / journal entry | **Mobile-first** | Post-mortem quick entry |
    22	| Journal browser | Desktop-first | Filter, R-distribution, history |
    23	| Edge review | Desktop-first | Per-setup stats, deactivation |
    24	| Risk rule editor | Desktop-only | Edit guardrail parameters |
    25	| Watchlist | Mobile + desktop | Candidates + triggers |
    26	| System health | Mobile + desktop | Token age, sync status, jobs, kill switch |
    27	
    28	## Flow 1: Morning glance (mobile, read-only)
    29	
    30	07:00 brief email → tap through → **Dashboard**.
    31	
    32	Dashboard states (mutually exclusive banners, one at a time):
    33	- **Healthy:** no banner.
    34	- **Token expiring:** refresh token < 24h. Banner links to re-auth flow.
    35	- **Token expired:** sync paused. Everything shows "as of [timestamp]" staleness marks. Re-auth is the only call to action.
    36	- **Halted:** daily-loss or drawdown rule tripped. Banner states which rule and when it resets. New-proposal entry points disabled, exits still available.
    37	
    38	Dashboard content: equity + day change, open positions (each: symbol, size, unrealized P&L, distance to stop as the primary number), total open risk ($ and % of equity), settled vs unsettled cash, pending proposal count (links to queue).
    39	
    40	Design constraint: distance-to-stop is the number that matters per position, not P&L. P&L is emotional; stop distance is actionable.
    41	
    42	## Flow 2: Review and approve a proposal (mobile-first, the core flow)
    43	
    44	Notification: "Proposal: BUY 40 XYZ @ 51.20, stop 48.90" → **Proposal detail**.
    45	
    46	Proposal detail sections, in order:
    47	1. The order: side, symbol, qty, type, limit, stop, target. Computed: risk $ if stopped, % of equity, position value.
    48	2. Thesis: the agent's (or your) one-paragraph reasoning, plus which setup it's tagged as.
    49	3. Guardrail results: one row per rule, each pass / warn / fail with the actual numbers ("Risk per trade: 0.9% of equity — pass, limit 1.0%"). Collar shown as a range with the proposed stop plotted inside/outside it.
    50	4. Action area (see states below).
    51	
    52	Proposal states → action area:
    53	- **All pass:** Approve and Reject buttons. Approve requires a deliberate confirm step (second tap on a changed button, or slide-to-confirm; your call, but not one-tap). This confirm is the moment the order goes to Schwab.
    54	- **Warn(s) present** (e.g., wash-sale flag): approve is available but each warning must be individually acknowledged first (tap to expand and acknowledge).
    55	- **Stop outside collar:** approve gated behind a required typed reason (logged). Show the collar bounds and where the stop sits.
    56	- **Hard fail** (GFV, notional cap, halt active): no approve control at all. The failing rule is stated with its numbers. Only actions: reject, or edit-and-resubmit (which creates a new proposal through the same validation).
    57	- **Approved → submitted → filled/cancelled:** read-only timeline view. Fill pushes a notification and links to the new journal row.
    58	
    59	Reject: optional one-line reason, stored on the proposal.
    60	
    61	## Flow 3: Manual proposal (human-initiated)
    62	
    63	**New proposal** form: symbol → live quote loads → entry, stop, target fields.
    64	
    65	Live feedback as the stop is typed:
    66	- Collar computes and renders as a range with the typed stop plotted against it.
    67	- Position size auto-computes from the risk rule (size = risk$ / (entry − stop)) and updates live.
    68	- Settled-cash check runs against the computed position value.
    69	
    70	Submit → same validation path and proposal detail screen as Flow 2. Human and agent proposals are identical objects downstream; the only difference is the author field.
    71	
    72	## Flow 4: Post-trade journal entry (mobile-first, 30-second task)
    73	
    74	Fill detected → journal row auto-created from transactions (entry/exit, R-multiple computed). EOD email lists rows missing post-mortems → tap → **Trade detail**.
    75	
    76	Entry is deliberately minimal: one-line post-mortem text field + one binary control: "Followed the setup / Improvised." Save. Everything else on the screen is read-only computed data (setup, planned vs actual stop, R-multiple).
    77	
    78	Rationale: if the journal entry takes more than 30 seconds on a phone, it stops happening.
    79	
    80	## Flow 5: Sunday ritual
    81	
    82	Sunday email contains: edge review summary, system health summary, re-auth button.
    83	
    84	- **Re-auth:** button → Schwab OAuth (their hosted login) → callback → success screen showing new token expiry date. Failure state: retry with the error shown.
    85	- **Edge review** screen: per-setup table (win rate, avg R, expectancy, sample size, trailing-20 trend). Setups with negative expectancy flagged. Action per setup: deactivate (confirm dialog stating the effect: agent stops proposing this setup). Reactivation same path.
    86	
    87	## Flow 6: Risk rule editing (desktop, rare, deliberate)
    88	
    89	List of rules with current parameters → edit one → before save, an effect preview: "Max risk 1.0% → 1.5% changes max position size at current equity from $X to $Y." Confirm to save. Every change is versioned with a timestamp (guardrail evaluations reference the rule version they ran against).
    90	
    91	No bulk edit. No editing while a halt is active (prevents mood-driven loosening on a bad day; the halt banner says so).
    92	
    93	## Flow 7: Watchlist
    94	
    95	List: symbol, trigger note ("break above 52.10 on volume"), added date, current price vs trigger. Add/edit/remove. The agent reads triggers; a trigger being met surfaces in the morning brief, not as a push (v1).
    96	
    97	## Flow 8: System health & kill switch
    98	
    99	Token age (days:hours, with the Sunday cadence marked), last successful sync per feed, recent job failures, API spend this month. One control: **Pause system** (kill switch): stops all proposal creation and submission until unpaused. Unpause requires typed confirmation.
   100	
   101	## Cross-cutting states
   102	
   103	Every screen handles:
   104	- **Stale data:** any market number older than its cache window shows a staleness mark with timestamp. Never render a price without its age being discoverable.
   105	- **Token expired:** global banner, read-only mode for anything requiring fresh Schwab data.
   106	- **Empty states:** pre-first-sync dashboard, empty journal, empty queue each need a designed state (the queue's empty state is the normal state most of the time).
   107	
   108	## Notification inventory (revised: push in the iOS app for time-sensitive items, email for long-form)
   109	
   110	Push (deep-link only, no figures in the payload): new proposal, fill/cancel, halt tripped, unprotected position, token expiring. Email: morning brief, EOD summary, Sunday ritual, job-failure digests. Original list:
   111	
   112	- Morning brief (07:00), EOD summary (16:30), Sunday ritual
   113	- New proposal awaiting review
   114	- Fill / cancel on a submitted order
   115	- Guardrail halt tripped

